# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""ncz-capability -- NCZ-OS hardware capability profiler, ranker and default selector.

One small, dependency-free tool that answers the operator's question
(2026-10-12): "hardware profile these machines and have an algorithm that ranks
systems by capability and only enables what they can healthily do by default."

It has three jobs:

  1. PROBE   collect the hardware facts (CPU, RAM, storage, GPUs, display,
             thermal/AC) and run a SHORT (<10 s) calibration: an offscreen GL
             fill+shader microbench, a CPU single/multi-thread microbench and a
             4k disk read-latency test.  Writes /etc/ncz/capability.json and a
             human summary on stdout.
  2. SCORE   turn the facts into per-subsystem subscores (0..100) and one tier
             (T0..T3) with a documented, deterministic function and explicit
             min-of-subsystem caps (a software renderer or a spinning disk caps
             the tier no matter how fast the CPU is).
  3. APPLY   write the tier's DEFAULTS (compositor effects, screensaver
             resolution/eligible set/fps, thermal governor trip points, boot
             splash mode, first-login tour, background indexer).  Defaults only:
             a user `gsettings set` still wins, and /etc/ncz/capability.override
             wins over the measured tier.

Tiers (names are free, the numbers are the contract):
  T0 minimal   T1 low   T2 mid   T3 high

Design: docs/CAPABILITY-TIERS.md.  Scoring is a pure function of the facts so it
is unit-testable (assets/capability/tests/test_capability.py) and the fleet
fixtures (assets/capability/fixtures/*.json) pin the tiers we validated on real
hardware.

Nothing here is destructive: apply only writes default files (a GSettings
override next to the installed schema, an /etc/environment.d file, a feature
file) and never touches a user's dconf values, never uninstalls and never masks
a unit for any tier above T0 (see the doc for the T0-only, reversible service
defaults).  Standard library only.
"""

